sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "ZFIN's \"clean\" phenotype file carries no experimental condition and is almost entirely standard conditions; 1034 attached abnormal rows whose annotation ZFIN also recorded under a treatment experiment, or that were uniquely non-standard, were dropped from \"required for\", and 2095 more came from dominant alleles without a truncating consequence, where loss of function is not established" ;
    dct:description "Status: serendipitous methodological finding, established by enumeration. phenoGeneCleanData_fish.txt carries a ZDB-GENOX id but no condition. Joining each row to phenotype_fish.txt (which carries the ZDB-EXP id) and pheno_environment_fish.txt (ZECO condition per experiment) shows that the clean file is almost entirely \"standard conditions\" (ZECO:0000103): over the whole file, 102 rows match one non-standard experiment uniquely and 2,914 match both a standard and a treatment experiment and cannot be told apart. Rule adopted: a row is kept only when every experiment it matches is standard conditions. Separately, a homozygous allele that also has an abnormal phenotype when heterozygous is dominant, and without a truncating consequence its loss of function is not established (the kcnk5b \"alf\" gain-of-function alleles are dominant missense), so such rows are rejected rather than typed \"required for\". Conditions among the candidate experiments of the dropped rows (standard conditions included, because most dropped rows are ambiguous): ZECO:0000103 standard conditions (1034); ZECO:0000238 chemical treatment by environment (541); ZECO:0000111 chemical treatment (122); ZECO:0000239 chemical treatment by diet (59); ZECO:0000237 chemical treatment by injection (53); ZECO:0000234 viral treatment by exposure to environment (31). What it does not establish: It does not show that the dropped rows are wrong; only that they are not loss-of-function phenotypes under standard conditions, which is what \"required for\" means here. Pre-registration: none: a data-cleaning gotcha; the rule was written in genotype/build.py before the vetted build." ;
    delphi:context "Abnormal rows 171714, attached to a blueprint node 45080. Loss-of-function evidence classes of kept rows: homozygous allele, recessive (no heterozygous phenotype recorded), consequence consequence not recorded in ZFIN: 9637; knockdown reagent (morpholino, CRISPR or TALEN): 13500; homozygous allele with a truncating or splice-site consequence (ZFIN features-affected-genes): 7496; homozygous allele, recessive (no heterozygous phenotype recorded), consequence missense or in-frame consequence only: 776; homozygous allele, recessive (no heterozygous phenotype recorded), consequence other consequence: 11; verified gain-of-function allele (hand-checked table GOF): 4; homozygous allele, recessive (no heterozygous phenotype recorded), consequence other consequence: 4; homozygous allele, recessive (no heterozygous phenotype recorded), consequence other consequence: 2." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Condition and dominance filtering of ZFIN phenotype rows" ;
    dct:description "Read from genotype/map.vetted.json summary.zfin_phenotype." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Join on fish, stages, publication, ontology ids and tag; counts by condition; no statistical test." ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/zfin-bulk-downloads-2026-10-31> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:map ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/genotype/data.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> schema:additionalProperty sub:m0 .
  sub:m0 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "status" ; schema:value "serendipitous methodological finding, established by enumeration" ; schema:description "status of this record in the words of AGENTS.md (supported, refuted, mixed, inconclusive, or a descriptive status)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> schema:additionalProperty sub:m1 .
  sub:m1 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "n_abnormal_rows" ; schema:value "171714"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "abnormal rows in the clean phenotype file" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> schema:additionalProperty sub:m2 .
  sub:m2 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "n_rows_attached_to_blueprint" ; schema:value "45080"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "rows attaching to a blueprint node through a cross-reference" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> schema:additionalProperty sub:m3 .
  sub:m3 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "n_rows_dropped_non_standard_or_ambiguous_condition" ; schema:value "1034"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "attached rows dropped because not every matching experiment was standard conditions (mostly ambiguous matches)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> schema:additionalProperty sub:m4 .
  sub:m4 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "n_rows_whole_file_uniquely_non_standard" ; schema:value "102"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "rows in the whole clean file that match exactly one experiment and it is non-standard (counted by the Genotype session on 2026-10-31, same join)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> schema:additionalProperty sub:m5 .
  sub:m5 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "n_rows_whole_file_ambiguous_standard_and_treatment" ; schema:value "2914"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "rows in the whole clean file that match both a standard and a treatment experiment (same count)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-zfin-clean-phenotype-file-conditions> schema:additionalProperty sub:m6 .
  sub:m6 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "n_rows_dropped_dominant_allele_lof_not_established" ; schema:value "2095"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "attached rows dropped: dominant allele without a truncating consequence" .
